 "text": "Annual Ethanol Production | Renewable Fuels Association\n\n# Annual Ethanol Production\n\nU.S. and World Ethanol Production\n\n## Annual Ethanol Production\n\n \n\n \n\nAnnual World Fuel Ethanol Production (Mil. Gal.)\n\n| Region | 2021 | 2022 | 2023 | 2024 | 2025 | % of World Production |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| United States | 15,016 | 15,361 | 15,580 | 16,225 | 16,494 | 52% |\n| Brazil | 7,240 | 7,400 | 8,610 | 8,980 | 8,650 | 27% |\n| India | 830 | 1,020 | 1,420 | 1,840 | 2,600 | 8% |\n| European Union | 1,380 | 1,430 | 1,410 | 1,480 | 1,500 | 5% |\n| China | 900 | 960 | 1,070 | 1,170 | 1,030 | 3% |\n| Canada | 434 | 447 | 454 | 464 | 472 | 1% |\n| Thailand | 350 | 380 | 360 | 360 | 390 | 1% |\n| Argentina | 270 | 310 | 310 | 310 | 330 | 1% |\n| Rest of World | 470 | 482 | 506 | 531 | 534 | 2% |\n| Total | 26,890 | 27,790 | 29,720 | 31,360 | 32,000 | |\n\n*Source: RFA analysis of public and private data sources\n\nAnnual U.S. Fuel Ethanol Production\n\n| Year | Million Gallons |\n| --- | --- |\n| 2015 | 14,807 |\n| 2016 | 15,413 |\n| 2017 | 15,936 |\n| 2018 | 16,091 |\n| 2019 | 15,778 |\n| 2020 | 13,941 |\n| 2021 | 15,016 |\n| 2022 | 15,361 |\n| 2023 | 15,580 |\n| 2024 | 16,225 |\n| 2025 | 16,494 |"
